		{
			"id": "tJokNBwFo6Sb6Tgw7",
			"name": "Chitin",
			"reference": "B46",
			"local_notes": "Placeholder entry at level 0. Every body-type lens below includes this trait with `levels` and `dr` overridden to its own anchor figure from framework.md's Tyranid table, and documents that lens's Weak Points rating and eye DR in its own copy of these notes: Tyranid chitin plating is organic and grows in overlapping but imperfect segments, with joints, sensory pits and eye clusters as the natural gaps a Weak Points roll represents.\n\nLore: A Tyranid's exoskeleton is grown, not worn: dense bio-ceramic chitin fused directly to the flesh beneath it, thickest on the largest bioforms and thin enough on a Termagant to be more like a swarm-trooper's flak jacket than real armour plate. Universal across Codex background and every piece of Black Library Tyranid fiction.\n\nDesign: Damage Resistance (B46, 5/level, all locations): natural DR bought directly on the body, per framework.md's explicit instruction that chitin is a character trait, not equipment. Each body-type lens overrides `levels`/`dr` to its own figure from framework.md's Tyranid anchor table; see that lens's own copy of this trait for its point cost.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"points_per_level": 5,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 0
		},
		{
			"id": "ti44H11zSPIDyopO-",
			"name": "Synapse Creature (Warrior)",
			"reference": "B35",
			"local_notes": "Every friendly Tyranid organism within 16 yards automatically gains Synapse Discipline's benefit and has Synapse Dependence suppressed, for as long as this creature is alive, conscious, and itself linked (directly or through a closer synapse creature) to the Hive Mind. A Tyranid Warrior's own Synapse Dependence is never active while it is drawing on the wider Hive Mind this way.\n\nLore: Tyranid Warriors are the swarm's front-line officers precisely because they project this field: Codex background across editions names Warriors, alongside larger synapse-capable bioforms, as the link that keeps a local swarm fighting with purpose instead of degenerating into a feeding frenzy the instant a fight turns bad.\n\nDesign: Affliction (B35) base 10; Advantage Delivered (a 10-point granted advantage, valued at +10% per this project's own Advantage/ Disadvantage Delivered convention); Area Effect at the 16-yard tier (+200%, B102); Always On (-40%, B113, it cannot be switched off); Emanation (-20%, B111, proximity only, no attack roll). Net: +10+200-40-20 = +150%. 10 x 2.5 = 25 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "m6P3e-eUNO8mCk5fl",
					"name": "Advantage Delivered (grants Synapse Discipline, 10 pts)",
					"cost_adj": "10%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mvVk1iBUYMNS_hG4r",
					"name": "Area Effect, 16 yards",
					"cost_adj": "+200%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mOFg-yDp2mdsLsfQe",
					"name": "Always On",
					"cost_adj": "-40%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mms4xYxsfT9zelToB",
					"name": "Emanation",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				}
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "tcVvJkt1BivHdAPBC",
			"name": "Synapse Creature (Zoanthrope)",
			"reference": "B35",
			"local_notes": "As the Tyranid Warrior's Synapse Creature trait, above: every friendly Tyranid organism within 16 yards gains Synapse Discipline and has Synapse Dependence suppressed while this Zoanthrope is alive, conscious, and linked to the Hive Mind.\n\nLore: Zoanthropes double as both psychic artillery and a mobile synapse node, a combination Codex background calls out explicitly as part of why they are escorted rather than left to operate alone.\n\nDesign: Identical build and math to the Tyranid Warrior's Synapse Creature trait, above (10 base, net +150%, 25 points) — a Zoanthrope's field is no wider than a Warrior's despite the psychic amplification that discipline goes into Shadow in the Warp instead.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "mXibuJZJDI3VSKYpN",
					"name": "Advantage Delivered (grants Synapse Discipline, 10 pts)",
					"cost_adj": "10%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mc1epmBSGmroh--9T",
					"name": "Area Effect, 16 yards",
					"cost_adj": "+200%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mP-WlMplkRarmLBDP",
					"name": "Always On",
					"cost_adj": "-40%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mIgIvaOFAQfy4RYIl",
					"name": "Emanation",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				}
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "tpc9woebcD1lpT69t",
			"name": "Synapse Creature (Hive Tyrant)",
			"reference": "B35",
			"local_notes": "As the Tyranid Warrior's Synapse Creature trait, but out to 32 yards: every friendly Tyranid organism in range gains Synapse Discipline and has Synapse Dependence suppressed while this Hive Tyrant is alive, conscious, and linked to the Hive Mind.\n\nLore: A Hive Tyrant is the Hive Mind's on-the-ground synapse lord: Codex background across editions gives it by far the largest synapse range of any single bioform, able to hold an entire local swarm together where a lone Warrior only holds a squad.\n\nDesign: Affliction (B35) base 10; Advantage Delivered (+10%); Area Effect at the 32-yard tier (+250%, B102); Always On (-40%); Emanation (-20%). Net: +10+250-40-20 = +200%. 10 x 3.0 = 30 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "madUe8PnSRVmPJGlN",
					"name": "Advantage Delivered (grants Synapse Discipline, 10 pts)",
					"cost_adj": "10%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mg9rwy36k2hYT5ctP",
					"name": "Area Effect, 32 yards",
					"cost_adj": "+250%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mA0StpQuTWLikpbJN",
					"name": "Always On",
					"cost_adj": "-40%"
				},
				{
					"id": "m0z1wluWtuptb-C9L",
					"name": "Emanation",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				}
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "ta1DXRfjhVTYzRQ76",
			"name": "Shadow in the Warp (Ravener)",
			"reference": "B35",
			"local_notes": "Any psyker (or other warp-sensitive mind) within 8 yards suffers -3 to Psyniscience, Warp Sorcery-tagged skill rolls, and the Will roll to resist Perils of the Warp, and must make an immediate Fright Check the first time they come within range of this creature. Non-psychic minds are unaffected.\n\nLore: The Hive Mind's raw psychic mass smothers the immaterium around any Tyranid bioform large enough to carry a fraction of it — Codex background describes Imperial and Aeldari psykers alike going deaf, blind, or outright panicking the moment a large Tyranid force (never just the smallest gaunts) comes close enough to sense. Deathwatch's Mark of the Xenos material treats Shadow in the Warp as a standing hazard for any Librarian escorting a kill-team against Tyranids.\n\nDesign: Affliction (B35) base 10; Disadvantage Delivered (a compound -30 point disadvantage — the skill/Empowerment penalty plus the forced Fright Check — valued per this project's own eyeballed Disadvantage Delivered convention, +30%); Area Effect at the 8-yard tier (+150%, B102); Always On (-40%); Emanation (-20%); Accessibility, limited to warp-sensitive targets only (-20%, the same kind of narrowing this project's Grey Knights Banishment entry uses for a daemon-only target restriction). Net: +30+150-40-20-20 = +100%. 10 x 2.0 = 20 points. Carried by the Ravener and Lictor as this project's own house choice (framework.md lists Shadow in the Warp as a Tyranid trait without saying which bioforms carry it); the Codex ties it to synapse creatures and the Hive Mind's psychic presence, which is why the Warrior, Zoanthrope and Hive Tyrant carry it and the mindless Carnifex does not.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "m-mV0hV84MwirmJoc",
					"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Warp-Deafened: -3 to psychic skill and Warp Empowerment-related rolls, plus an immediate Fright Check on first exposure, -30 pts)",
					"cost_adj": "30%"
				},
				{
					"id": "m1lFp5rTU0nRKNypf",
					"name": "Area Effect, 8 yards",
					"cost_adj": "+150%"
				},
				{
