					"base_points": 0
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "T1ypFqhNYXMynWfXx",
			"name": "Body Lens: Lictor",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Lictor: a solitary, chameleonic stalker sent ahead of a landing to scout, terrorise, and mark a kill zone for the swarm that follows -- consistent Codex background across editions, and the basis for the classic \"something was watching, then it wasn't\" Black Library beat.\n\nDesign: 352 (Attribute Modifiers) + 300 (Chitin DR 60) + 20 (Chameleonic Hide) + 20 (Clinging) + 1 (Pheromone Trail) + 20 (Shadow in the Warp) + 50 (Injury Tolerance 2) = 763 points, added to Tyranid Biology's 20 for 763 points of physiology alone before skills and its weapon-symbiotes, about 40 points above the Tyranid Warrior lens (ST 36 against 34). See the Lictor template. NPC creature stat block only.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tM0zDXBdPupqc821P",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Lictor)",
					"local_notes": "Design: Framework target: SM +1, ST 36, DX 15, IQ 8, HT 13, HP 40. Increased ST +26 (260) for ST 36 (strength ladder: level with a Skorpekh Destroyer) with the SM +1 discount: 260 x 0.9 = 234. Increased DX +5 (B15, 20/level, 100) for DX 15 -- a stalking ambush predator with the swarm's best reflexes outside a Genestealer's. Decreased IQ -2 (-40) for IQ 8, sharp enough for patient, solo infiltration work rather than raw instinct. Increased HT +3 (30) for HT 13. Extra Hit Points +4 (8) on top of the ST-36 base of 36, for HP 40. Increased Basic Move +4 (B17, 5/level, 20): Basic Speed 7.0 gives Move 7, so +4 lands Basic Move at 11. 234+100-40+30+8+20 = 352.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical"
					],
					"base_points": 352,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "sm",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": 26
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "dx",
							"amount": 5
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "iq",
							"amount": -2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "ht",
							"amount": 3
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "hp",
							"amount": 4
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "basic_move",
							"amount": 4
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tmPTKhh_1wuqwoJsc",
					"name": "Chitin (Lictor)",
					"reference": "B46",
					"local_notes": "DR 60, all locations. Weak Points 5 (as a Ravener's or Warrior's, matching framework.md's own figure for this tier): on a hit that fails to penetrate, roll 3d; 5 or less halves DR (30). Eye clusters run at DR 30 rather than 60.\n\nLore: A Tyranid's exoskeleton is grown, not worn: dense bio-ceramic chitin fused directly to the flesh beneath it, thickest on the largest bioforms and thin enough on a Termagant to be more like a swarm-trooper's flak jacket than real armour plate. Universal across Codex background and every piece of Black Library Tyranid fiction.\n\nDesign: Damage Resistance (B46, 5/level, all locations): natural DR bought directly on the body, per framework.md's explicit instruction that chitin is a character trait, not equipment. Each body-type lens overrides `levels`/`dr` to its own figure from framework.md's Tyranid anchor table; see that lens's own copy of this trait for its point cost.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 60,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "dr_bonus",
							"locations": [
								"all"
							],
							"amount": 60
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "td_jrt4yLzrzLyszE",
					"name": "Chameleonic Hide",
					"reference": "B41",
					"local_notes": "-4 to others' Vision rolls to spot the Lictor while it is motionless, or -2 while moving (per Basic's Chameleon rule, B41); does not work against Infravision, scent-based tracking, or other non-visual detection.\n\nLore: A Lictor's hide shifts colour and texture to match its surroundings well enough to stand motionless in plain sight and go unnoticed until it strikes — the bioform's whole reason for existing in Codex background, and the source of its reputation as the swarm's perfect assassin in Black Library's Hive Fleet fiction.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Chameleon (B41/P43, 5 points/level), level 4, 20 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 4
				},
				{
					"id": "tULSQ5pGNOqMCKKVF",
					"name": "Clinging",
					"reference": "B43",
					"local_notes": "Walks or crawls up walls and across ceilings at half Move, no Climbing roll.\n\nLore: Genestealers and Lictors move through a ruin as easily up its walls as along its floor: Space Hulk's broods come out of the ceiling vents, and the Lictor waits on the underside of a gantry or the face of a hab-block until its prey walks beneath. Codex background has both scale sheer surfaces with hooked claws and barbed limbs.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Clinging (B43, 20 points), unmodified.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"base_points": 20
				},
				{
					"id": "tRYxsJ15iOpZipsiT",
					"name": "Pheromone Trail",
					"local_notes": "Automatically marks the Lictor's path and kill sites with a chemical trail other Tyranid organisms can follow without a roll, for as long as roughly a day; the GM may use this to have the nearest swarm elements arrive at a Lictor's last known location once its scouting or killing is done.\n\nLore: Lictors scout ahead of a landing and leave a chemical trail for the rest of the Hive Fleet to follow to a viable kill zone — standard Codex background on the bioform's actual battlefield purpose (infiltration and target-marking, not sustained combat).\n\nDesign: Perk (B21, 1 point): a narrow, always-on tracking convenience for other Tyranids rather than a combat effect, priced the same way this project's other Perk-tier flavour traits (Necron's \"Beneath a Daemon's Notice,\" this file's own Klan-style flags) are.",
					"tags": [
						"Perk",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"base_points": 1
				},
				{
					"id": "twF40Gjxct2mmeW5r",
					"name": "Shadow in the Warp (Lictor)",
					"reference": "B35",
					"local_notes": "As the Ravener's Shadow in the Warp trait, above: 8-yard radius, -3 to psychic rolls, forced Fright Check on first exposure.\n\nLore: A Lictor is large enough to carry the same psychic weight as any other mid-tier bioform, on top of everything else that makes it a nightmare to hunt.\n\nDesign: Identical build and math to the Ravener's Shadow in the Warp trait, above (20 points).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mzNIUayrIdxP2GW1S",
							"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Warp-Deafened: -3 to psychic skill and Warp Empowerment-related rolls, plus an immediate Fright Check on first exposure, -30 pts)",
							"cost_adj": "30%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mRBqZeSYsJsqduAuS",
