		{
			"id": "TPk0QyjwriT5Bu7lj",
			"name": "Body Lens: Zoanthrope",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Zoanthrope: a dedicated psychic amplifier for the Hive Mind, floating on its own telekinetic field and doubling as a synapse node -- consistent Codex background across editions, and Black Library's few Zoanthrope-focussed scenes always frame it as artillery to be escorted, not a front-line fighter.\n\nDesign: 24 (Attribute Modifiers) + 200 (Chitin DR 40) + 100 (Warp Field) + 25 (Synapse Creature) + 25 (Shadow in the Warp) = 374 points, added to Tyranid Biology's 20 for 394 points of physiology alone before skills and Warp Blast (data/xenos/tyranids/psychic.yaml). See the Zoanthrope template. NPC creature stat block only.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tjOK4Hw3LAZ2NCOsD",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Zoanthrope)",
					"local_notes": "Design: Framework target: SM +1, ST 8, DX 10, IQ 10, HT 12, HP 20. Decreased ST -2 (B14, 10/level, -20) for ST 8 -- a floating, near-vestigial body; no SM discount is taken on a decrease, per this project's own Termagant/Hormagaunt precedent. DX 10 is human baseline (0 points). IQ 10 is human baseline (0 points) -- smart enough to channel real psychic power but no genius. Increased HT +2 (B15, 10/level, 20) for HT 12. Extra Hit Points +12 (B16, 2/level, 24) on top of the ST-8 base of 8, for HP 20 -- a huge Extra HP purchase reflecting a body that is nearly all brain and psychic organ, propped up by bulk rather than muscle. -20+20+24 = 24.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical"
					],
					"base_points": 24,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "sm",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": -2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "ht",
							"amount": 2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "hp",
							"amount": 12
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tfL6gE48F10saHceS",
					"name": "Chitin (Zoanthrope)",
					"reference": "B46",
					"local_notes": "DR 40, all locations. Weak Points 6 (a soft, floating body with only partial plating, gappier than a ground-fighting bioform of similar DR): on a hit that fails to penetrate, roll 3d; 6 or less halves DR (20). Eye clusters run at DR 20 rather than 40. See the Warp Field trait, below, for the psychic shield that sits in front of this DR.\n\nLore: A Tyranid's exoskeleton is grown, not worn: dense bio-ceramic chitin fused directly to the flesh beneath it, thickest on the largest bioforms and thin enough on a Termagant to be more like a swarm-trooper's flak jacket than real armour plate. Universal across Codex background and every piece of Black Library Tyranid fiction.\n\nDesign: Damage Resistance (B46, 5/level, all locations): natural DR bought directly on the body, per framework.md's explicit instruction that chitin is a character trait, not equipment. Each body-type lens overrides `levels`/`dr` to its own figure from framework.md's Tyranid anchor table; see that lens's own copy of this trait for its point cost.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 40,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "dr_bonus",
							"locations": [
								"all"
							],
							"amount": 40
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tuhVSYGUjjh4_zXBQ",
					"name": "Warp Field (Bio-Psychic Ward)",
					"local_notes": "A regenerating psychic buffer, built on the same Shield Points mechanic framework.md's \"Personal force fields\" section uses for worn refractor fields and the like: SP 200, 2-second delay, recharges 25 SP/second once undamaged for that long, covers all locations. Damage comes off this pool first (armour divisors do not apply to SP); once it is exhausted, excess damage carries on to the Zoanthrope's chitin at the attack's full armour divisor, and the field needs a full 4 seconds undamaged before it starts recharging from empty. Track current SP with a Uses counter, as for worn fields.\n\nLore: A Zoanthrope generates a visible, crackling field of raw psychic force around its frail body — its only real protection beyond its own thin chitin, and Codex background's explanation for why a Zoanthrope can survive fire that would kill it outright without one. On the tabletop it has long been one of the best invulnerable saves in the game (3+ for most editions), better than a Terminator's storm shield, so bolter and lasgun fire spatters off it and only massed or heavy weapons break through.\n\nDesign: This project has no published point-cost formula for a shield's SP pool (framework.md tracks worn fields as equipment with a Uses counter, not as a priced character trait); a Zoanthrope's field is part of its body rather than worn gear, so it needs an honest point price here. Eyeballed at half of Damage Resistance's own rate (B46, 5 points per point of permanent DR) for a pool that absorbs the same amount of damage but is temporary and must recharge, i.e. 0.5 points per SP: 200 SP x 0.5 = 100 points. Raised from 60 SP (30 points, the Rosarius anchor) at the user's direction, because 60 SP broke to two bolts and the lore field outlasts a storm shield: 200 SP sits above framework.md's storm shield (160 SP, 20/s) and recharges at 25 SP/second, so a squad's bolters must keep firing to wear it down, while a lascannon (8dx8(5), about 224) still breaks it in one shot. The 4-second restart after collapse is kept. This is a reasoned extrapolation from Basic Set principles, not a catalogue trait renamed, and a future framework update that adds a formal shield- point pricing formula should supersede it.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"base_points": 100
				},
				{
					"id": "tjpMwAiJ2CfOHjH1L",
					"name": "Synapse Creature (Zoanthrope)",
					"reference": "B35",
					"local_notes": "As the Tyranid Warrior's Synapse Creature trait, above: every friendly Tyranid organism within 16 yards gains Synapse Discipline and has Synapse Dependence suppressed while this Zoanthrope is alive, conscious, and linked to the Hive Mind.\n\nLore: Zoanthropes double as both psychic artillery and a mobile synapse node, a combination Codex background calls out explicitly as part of why they are escorted rather than left to operate alone.\n\nDesign: Identical build and math to the Tyranid Warrior's Synapse Creature trait, above (10 base, net +150%, 25 points) — a Zoanthrope's field is no wider than a Warrior's despite the psychic amplification that discipline goes into Shadow in the Warp instead.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "m-p6XeEETrA69EVMo",
							"name": "Advantage Delivered (grants Synapse Discipline, 10 pts)",
