							"id": "mht2N_rbFq9do-Sa7",
							"name": "Always On",
							"cost_adj": "-40%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mq-MQLgpC6Er7o2aC",
							"name": "Emanation",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mQIITqVKV4yCkObIf",
							"name": "Accessibility (only affects psykers and other warp-sensitive minds)",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 10
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TLEbl7Ul11OOqSYyZ",
			"name": "Body Lens: Hive Tyrant",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Hive Tyrant: the Hive Mind's synapse lord and its own psyker, the biggest single command bioform normally seen on the ground and the anchor of a swarm's local tactical will. Consistent Codex background across editions; Black Library's Hive Fleet fiction routinely treats a confirmed Hive Tyrant kill as a campaign-level victory.\n\nDesign: 943 (Attribute Modifiers) + 750 (Chitin DR 150) + 25 (Regeneration) + 10 (High Pain Threshold) + 30 (Synapse Creature) + 30 (Shadow in the Warp) + 75 (Injury Tolerance 3) = 1863 points (Wings disabled by default, +30 more if enabled), added to Tyranid Biology's 20 for 1345 points of physiology alone before skills, psychic powers (data/xenos/tyranids/psychic.yaml) and weapon- symbiotes -- squarely in framework.md's Heroes and Legends tier (1,000-3,000), appropriate for the swarm's synapse lord. See the Hive Tyrant template. NPC creature stat block only; this total is for GM reference, not party balance.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "ts_9RhEHmqX1sX1v5",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Hive Tyrant)",
					"local_notes": "Design: Framework target: SM +2, ST 100, DX 13, IQ 12, HT 16, HP 130 (user direction: tougher; it was ST 55, HP 70). Increased ST +90 (B14, 10/level, 900) for ST 100, with the SM +2 discount (-10% per point of positive SM, per B18, the same rate this project's Ork Warboss and Custodes entries use, here two steps): 900 x 0.8 = 720. Increased DX +3 (60) for DX 13. Increased IQ +2 (B16, 20/level, 40) for IQ 12 -- a genuine synapse lord and psyker, sharper than any lesser bioform. Increased HT +6 (B15, 10/level, 60) for HT 16. Extra Hit Points +30 (B16, 2/level, with the SM discount: 60 x 0.8 = 48) on top of the ST-100 base, for HP 130, inside Pyramid 3/77's \"within 30% of ST\". Increased Basic Move +3 (B17, 5/level, 15): Basic Speed 7.25 gives Move 7, so +3 lands Basic Move at 10. 720+60+40+60+48+15 = 943.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical"
					],
					"base_points": 943,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "sm",
							"amount": 2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": 90
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "dx",
							"amount": 3
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "iq",
							"amount": 2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "ht",
							"amount": 6
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "hp",
							"amount": 30
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "basic_move",
							"amount": 3
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tWT0XOoespqg15lkt",
					"name": "Chitin (Hive Tyrant)",
					"reference": "B46",
					"local_notes": "DR 150, all locations (user direction: tougher; was 120), level with the Carnifex. Weak Points 4 (a synapse lord's plating is thicker and better-grown than a rank-and-file predator's): on a hit that fails to penetrate, roll 3d; 4 or less halves DR (75).\n\nLore: A Tyranid's exoskeleton is grown, not worn: dense bio-ceramic chitin fused directly to the flesh beneath it, thickest on the largest bioforms and thin enough on a Termagant to be more like a swarm-trooper's flak jacket than real armour plate. Universal across Codex background and every piece of Black Library Tyranid fiction.\n\nDesign: Damage Resistance (B46, 5/level, all locations): natural DR bought directly on the body, per framework.md's explicit instruction that chitin is a character trait, not equipment. Each body-type lens overrides `levels`/`dr` to its own figure from framework.md's Tyranid anchor table; see that lens's own copy of this trait for its point cost.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 150,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "dr_bonus",
							"locations": [
								"all"
							],
							"amount": 150
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "t3jwGWiTBTOPgIhvD",
					"name": "Regeneration (Adapted Biomass)",
					"reference": "B80",
					"local_notes": "Regeneration (Regular): recovers 1 HP per hour even without rest or first aid.\n\nLore: Larger Tyranid bioforms visibly close wounds and regrow damaged tissue over the course of a battle, part of the same adaptive biology that lets the Hive Fleet field bioforms built to take punishment no unaugmented creature could survive. Codex background across editions gives this trait explicitly to Tyranid monstrous creatures.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Regeneration (Regular) (B80, 25 points).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"base_points": 25
				},
				{
					"id": "tqA1IEwVbKG80voEJ",
					"name": "High Pain Threshold",
					"reference": "B59",
					"local_notes": "No shock penalties; +3 to HT rolls to avoid knockdown and stunning.\n\nLore: The synapse lord is the swarm's \"no pain\"; it feels its wounds no more than its brood does.\n\nDesign: Basic Set High Pain Threshold (B59), 10 points (user direction, tougher).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "t6ZgEZGm1E3GiNded",
					"name": "Wings (Flight)",
					"reference": "B56",
					"local_notes": "Disabled by default; enable for a winged Hive Tyrant variant. Air Move equals twice Basic Speed (dropping fractions), per Basic's Flight rule; Winged flight cannot hover and is grounded by high winds or a damaged wing, same as any other winged flier.\n\nLore: Some Hive Tyrants are grown with a huge, membranous wing pair for genuine flight rather than the leaping glides other large bioforms manage — a well-known wargear/bioform option across Codex editions and a striking image in Black Library's Hive Fleet material whenever a Winged Hive Tyrant appears.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Flight (B56, 40 points) with the Winged limitation (-25%, B56, cannot hover, grounded by bad weather or wing damage): 40 x 0.75 = 30 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mIVWqlu7QK-48Vvk_",
							"name": "Winged",
							"reference": "B56",
							"cost_adj": "-25%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 40,
					"disabled": true
				},
				{
					"id": "tyUxtZR6F8viX4lNN",
					"name": "Synapse Creature (Hive Tyrant)",
					"reference": "B35",
					"local_notes": "As the Tyranid Warrior's Synapse Creature trait, but out to 32 yards: every friendly Tyranid organism in range gains Synapse Discipline and has Synapse Dependence suppressed while this Hive Tyrant is alive, conscious, and linked to the Hive Mind.\n\nLore: A Hive Tyrant is the Hive Mind's on-the-ground synapse lord: Codex background across editions gives it by far the largest synapse range of any single bioform, able to hold an entire local swarm together where a lone Warrior only holds a squad.\n\nDesign: Affliction (B35) base 10; Advantage Delivered (+10%); Area Effect at the 32-yard tier (+250%, B102); Always On (-40%); Emanation (-20%). Net: +10+250-40-20 = +200%. 10 x 3.0 = 30 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mWVO5FIoF7-J7-kC9",
							"name": "Advantage Delivered (grants Synapse Discipline, 10 pts)",
							"cost_adj": "10%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mvvzX5WB_kXqOisWs",
							"name": "Area Effect, 32 yards",
							"cost_adj": "+250%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mNND1aJcT6GKxhRZB",
							"name": "Always On",
							"cost_adj": "-40%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mVKT-ed0-C5JLbwc5",
							"name": "Emanation",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "tswaACFL7KvHKAa0H",
					"name": "Shadow in the Warp (Hive Tyrant)",
					"reference": "B35",
					"local_notes": "Any psyker within 32 yards suffers -3 to Psyniscience, Warp Sorcery-tagged skill rolls, and the Will roll to resist Perils of the Warp, and must make an immediate Fright Check the first time they come within range.\n\nLore: A Hive Tyrant carries the largest single share of the Hive Mind's psychic mass of any bioform on the ground, matching its synapse range with the widest Shadow in the Warp in this file.\n\nDesign: Affliction (B35) base 10; Disadvantage Delivered (+30%); Area Effect at the 32-yard tier (+250%, B102); Always On (-40%); Emanation (-20%); Accessibility (-20%). Net: +30+250-40-20-20 = +200%. 10 x 3.0 = 30 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "m1kVpIrXo4ijF2HiK",
							"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Warp-Deafened: -3 to psychic skill and Warp Empowerment-related rolls, plus an immediate Fright Check on first exposure, -30 pts)",
							"cost_adj": "30%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mtNNAsQTKVrvsjXZg",
							"name": "Area Effect, 32 yards",
							"cost_adj": "+250%"
						},
						{
							"id": "myiSNdj75AXKU5jjz",
							"name": "Always On",
							"cost_adj": "-40%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mIr77PTSx-Pr8Nr8-",
							"name": "Emanation",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mkSfDUjdfWDvGB9kL",
							"name": "Accessibility (only affects psykers and other warp-sensitive minds)",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "tVAWIAobc9Oi1j3Y3",
					"name": "Injury Tolerance (Damage Reduction)",
					"reference": "P53",
					"local_notes": "Divisor 3 (level = divisor): after DR and wounding multipliers, all injury is divided by 3 (round down, minimum 1 if anything penetrated).\n\nLore: A Hive Tyrant's vast bulk and redundant organs make a killing wound very hard to land. Large synapse-beasts and monsters shrug off wounds that would fell smaller creatures.\n\nDesign: Injury Tolerance (Damage Reduction) (GURPS Powers p. 53, 25 points per level, level = divisor): divisor 3 = 75 points. Gives the Hive Tyrant the bulk-and-redundant-organs toughness the lore describes on top of its chitin DR and extra HP.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"points_per_level": 25,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 3,
					"base_points": 0
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "Tiir8F939ijoMA5vj",
			"name": "Body Lens: Carnifex",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Carnifex: a living battering ram grown purely to soak up and deal out damage that would kill anything else outright, deployed wherever the swarm needs a hole punched through armour, fortification or a defensive line. Consistent Codex background across editions and Black Library's Hive Fleet fiction alike.\n\nDesign: 883 (Attribute Modifiers) + 750 (Chitin DR 150) + 50 (Regeneration, Fast) + 15 (Unfazeable) + 10 (High Pain Threshold) + 75 (Injury Tolerance 3) = 1783 points, added to Tyranid Biology's 20 for 1803 points of physiology alone before skills and weapon-symbiotes -- squarely in framework.md's Heroes and Legends tier (1,000-3,000), matching a Hive Tyrant's own physiology cost almost exactly despite the very different build (raw ST and DR instead of IQ, synapse range and wings; now well above it at ST 120). See the Carnifex template. NPC creature stat block only; this total is for GM reference, not party balance.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tK88yosW9Bqt8-kpg",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Carnifex)",
					"local_notes": "Design: Framework target: SM +2, ST 120, DX 10, IQ 4, HT 16, HP 120. Increased ST +110 (B14, 10/level, 1,100) for ST 120, with the SM +2 discount: 1,100 x 0.8 = 880. ST 120 (user direction: a Carnifex should flip a tank with little struggle; Basic Lift 2,880 lb, and its two-handed shove or lift handles a light vehicle). DX 10 is human baseline (0 points) -- a Carnifex is not precise, it is simply unstoppable. Decreased IQ -6 (B16, 20/level, -120) for IQ 4, as debased as a Termagant's -- pure directed muscle. Increased HT +6 (60) for HT 16. HP 150 (user direction: tougher): the ST-120 base plus Extra Hit Points +30 (B16, 2/level, with the SM +2 discount: 60 x 0.8 = 48), at the top of Pyramid 3/77's \"HP within 30% of ST\". Increased Basic Move +3 (B17, 5/level, 15): Basic Speed 6.5 gives Move 6, so +3 lands Basic Move at 9. 880-120+60+48+15 = 883.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical"
					],
					"base_points": 883,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "sm",
							"amount": 2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": 110
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "iq",
							"amount": -6
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "ht",
							"amount": 6
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "hp",
							"amount": 30
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "basic_move",
							"amount": 3
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "t_AODgFRVhzGtstX0",
					"name": "Chitin (Carnifex)",
					"reference": "B46",
					"local_notes": "DR 150, all locations -- the anchor's own top figure. Weak Points 3 (the thickest, least gappy chitin any Tyranid grows, on a par with Terminator plate): on a hit that fails to penetrate, roll 3d; 3 or less halves DR (75). Eye clusters run at DR 75 rather than 150.\n\nLore: A Tyranid's exoskeleton is grown, not worn: dense bio-ceramic chitin fused directly to the flesh beneath it, thickest on the largest bioforms and thin enough on a Termagant to be more like a swarm-trooper's flak jacket than real armour plate. Universal across Codex background and every piece of Black Library Tyranid fiction.\n\nDesign: Damage Resistance (B46, 5/level, all locations): natural DR bought directly on the body, per framework.md's explicit instruction that chitin is a character trait, not equipment. Each body-type lens overrides `levels`/`dr` to its own figure from framework.md's Tyranid anchor table; see that lens's own copy of this trait for its point cost.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 150,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "dr_bonus",
							"locations": [
								"all"
							],
							"amount": 150
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "t0gYndUryMTstvzib",
					"name": "Regeneration (Adapted Biomass, Fast)",
					"reference": "B80",
					"local_notes": "Regeneration (Fast): recovers 1 HP per minute even without rest or first aid.\n\nLore: A Carnifex is built to absorb an amount of damage that would kill any other bioform several times over and keep coming, closing wounds visibly fast enough to matter mid-fight — Codex background's consistent framing of the Carnifex as the swarm's most durable single-target answer to armour.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Regeneration (Fast) (B80, 50 points), one tier above the Hive Tyrant's Regular rate, matching the Carnifex's specific reputation for shrugging off damage that would down a Hive Tyrant.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"base_points": 50
				},
				{
					"id": "tOUYvc1OjE55T7A5G",
					"name": "Unfazeable",
					"reference": "B95",
					"local_notes": "No Fright Checks; nothing frightens a mindless siege beast.\n\nLore: A Carnifex does not know fear; it knows the next wall, the next tank, the next squad.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Unfazeable (B95), 15 points (user direction, tougher).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"base_points": 15
				},
				{
					"id": "tka4xpBUsdhHsmD-h",
					"name": "High Pain Threshold",
					"reference": "B59",
					"local_notes": "No shock penalties; +3 to HT rolls to avoid knockdown and stunning.\n\nLore: The swarm's \"no pain\" made flesh; a Carnifex keeps coming through wounds that would drop a tank crew.\n\nDesign: Basic Set High Pain Threshold (B59), 10 points (user direction, tougher).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"base_points": 10
